## Selection Sort

### 📌 Problem Description
Implement the Selection Sort algorithm to sort an array of integers in ascending order.

### 💡 Approach
1. Start from the first index of the array.
2. Find the index of the minimum element in the unsorted portion of the array.
3. Swap the minimum element with the element at the current index.
4. Move to the next index and repeat the process until the entire array is sorted.

### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis
- **Time Complexity:** O(n²) in the best, average, and worst cases.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1), as sorting is performed in place.

### 🛠️ Language
Java

###Solution

class Solution {
    public int[] selectionSort(int[] nums) {
        // Handle edge case
        if (nums == null || nums.length <= 1) {
            return nums;
        }
        
        int n = nums.length;
        
        // One by one move the boundary of the unsorted subarray
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            // Find the minimum element in the unsorted array
            int minIdx = i;
            for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
                if (nums[j] < nums[minIdx]) {
                    minIdx = j;
                }
            }
            
            // Swap the found minimum element with the first element of the unsorted part
            int temp = nums[minIdx];
            nums[minIdx] = nums[i];
            nums[i] = temp;
        }
        
        return nums;
    }
}
